# serializer version: 1
# name: test_command_help_text[command0]
  '''
  usage: sci2audio script [-h] [-o FOLDER] [--chapters LIST] [--on CATEGORY]
                          [--off CATEGORY] [--language TAG] [--overwrite]
                          [--work-folder FOLDER] [--ignore-settings] [-q]
                          FILE
  
  Read FILE and write what the voice would say (FILE.script.txt) and the report
  of every change (FILE.report.json, FILE.report.md). Lists the chapters to
  choose from.
  
  positional arguments:
    FILE                  the file to read
  
  options:
    -h, --help            show this help message and exit
    -o FOLDER, --output FOLDER
                          where the files go (default: next to FILE)
    --chapters LIST       chapters to read, counted from 1 as `script` lists
                          them: 1,3-5 or all (default: every chapter but the
                          reference list)
    --on CATEGORY         switch a text-step category on (repeat, or separate
                          with commas)
    --off CATEGORY        switch a text-step category off: its text is read as
                          printed
    --language TAG        en, en-GB, ... (default: the file's own, else guessed
                          from the text: en or de)
    --overwrite           replace existing output files
    --work-folder FOLDER  the job's working folder (default: in the cache
                          folder)
    --ignore-settings     use the built-in defaults, not the settings saved by
                          the interface
    -q, --quiet           no progress lines
  
  text-step categories (for --on and --off):
    page-furniture       Page furniture (starts on)
    characters           Characters and hyphenation (starts on)
    footnotes            Footnotes (starts on)
    footnote-texts       Footnote texts (starts off)
    citations            Citations (starts on)
    links                URLs, DOIs and e-mail addresses (starts on)
    formulas             Formulas (starts on)
    tables-and-figures   Tables and figures (starts on)
    references           Reference list (starts on)
    abbreviations        Abbreviations (starts on)
    numbers-and-units    Numbers, symbols, units and statistics (starts on)
    "on" means sci2audio handles that kind of text (e.g. citations are left out);
    "off" means it is read as printed.
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_command_help_text[command1]
  '''
  usage: sci2audio convert [-h] [-o FOLDER] [--chapters LIST] [--on CATEGORY]
                           [--off CATEGORY] [--language TAG] [--overwrite]
                           [--work-folder FOLDER] [--ignore-settings] [-q]
                           [--voice ID] [--speed X] [--format {both,m4b,mp3}]
                           [--with-script] [--models-folder FOLDER]
                           FILE
  
  Make the audiobook of FILE. Running the same command again continues an
  interrupted run: sentences already spoken are taken from the speech cache.
  
  positional arguments:
    FILE                  the file to read
  
  options:
    -h, --help            show this help message and exit
    -o FOLDER, --output FOLDER
                          where the files go (default: next to FILE)
    --chapters LIST       chapters to read, counted from 1 as `script` lists
                          them: 1,3-5 or all (default: every chapter but the
                          reference list)
    --on CATEGORY         switch a text-step category on (repeat, or separate
                          with commas)
    --off CATEGORY        switch a text-step category off: its text is read as
                          printed
    --language TAG        en, en-GB, ... (default: the file's own, else guessed
                          from the text: en or de)
    --overwrite           replace existing output files
    --work-folder FOLDER  the job's working folder (default: in the cache
                          folder)
    --ignore-settings     use the built-in defaults, not the settings saved by
                          the interface
    -q, --quiet           no progress lines
    --voice ID            a voice from `sci2audio voices` (default: af_heart)
    --speed X             0.5 to 2.0 (default: 1.0)
    --format {both,m4b,mp3}
                          M4B with chapter marks, one MP3 per chapter, or both
                          (default: both)
    --with-script         also write the listening script and the report
    --models-folder FOLDER
                          where the voice files are (default: in the user's data
                          folder)
  
  text-step categories (for --on and --off):
    page-furniture       Page furniture (starts on)
    characters           Characters and hyphenation (starts on)
    footnotes            Footnotes (starts on)
    footnote-texts       Footnote texts (starts off)
    citations            Citations (starts on)
    links                URLs, DOIs and e-mail addresses (starts on)
    formulas             Formulas (starts on)
    tables-and-figures   Tables and figures (starts on)
    references           Reference list (starts on)
    abbreviations        Abbreviations (starts on)
    numbers-and-units    Numbers, symbols, units and statistics (starts on)
    "on" means sci2audio handles that kind of text (e.g. citations are left out);
    "off" means it is read as printed.
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_command_help_text[command2]
  '''
  usage: sci2audio voices [-h] [--models-folder FOLDER] ACTION ...
  
  List the voices and whether their files are installed. `voices download` shows
  what it fetches and asks before anything is downloaded.
  
  positional arguments:
    ACTION
      download            download the voice files (about 680 MB), after showing
                          what and asking
  
  options:
    -h, --help            show this help message and exit
    --models-folder FOLDER
                          where the voice files are (default: in the user's data
                          folder)
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_command_help_text[command3]
  '''
  usage: sci2audio voices download [-h] [--models-folder FOLDER] [-y]
                                   [--language {en,de}]
  
  Download the voice files: the Kokoro model with its English voices and the
  spaCy English model (about 355 MB), and the German Kokoro model with the voice
  Thorsten (about 330 MB). Shows every source, size and licence first, then
  asks.
  
  options:
    -h, --help            show this help message and exit
    --models-folder FOLDER
                          where the voice files are (default: in the user's data
                          folder)
    -y, --yes             agree to the download without being asked
    --language {en,de}    only the voice files of this language; repeat for more
                          (default: every language)
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_command_help_text[command4]
  '''
  usage: sci2audio clean [-h] [--work-folder FOLDER] FILE
  
  Remove the speech cache of FILE (the spoken sentences kept for a quick rerun).
  The audiobook and the records stay.
  
  positional arguments:
    FILE                  the file whose speech cache goes
  
  options:
    -h, --help            show this help message and exit
    --work-folder FOLDER  the job's working folder (default: in the cache
                          folder)
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_command_help_text[command5]
  '''
  usage: sci2audio ui [-h] [--no-browser]
  
  Start the sci2audio interface on this computer (127.0.0.1 only) and open it in
  your browser. Press Ctrl-C to stop it.
  
  options:
    -h, --help    show this help message and exit
    --no-browser  only print the link; do not open a browser
  
  '''
# ---
# name: test_help_text
  '''
  usage: sci2audio [-h] [--version] COMMAND ...
  
  Turn scientific texts into faithful, offline audiobooks.
  
  positional arguments:
    COMMAND
      script    write the listening script and the report (no voice needed)
      convert   make the audiobook: an M4B with chapters, an MP3 per chapter and
                a read-along file
      voices    list the voices; `voices download` installs their files
      clean     remove the speech cache of FILE
      ui        open the sci2audio interface in your browser (it stays on this
                computer)
  
  options:
    -h, --help  show this help message and exit
    --version   show program's version number and exit
  
  exit codes:
    0    done (problems listed in the report do not change it)
    1    failed for another reason (a write, the disk, ffmpeg, the voice, the download)
    2    a bad option or value
    3    the file does not exist or is not a file
    4    a file type sci2audio can't read
    5    the file is damaged, protected or can't be opened
    6    the voice files are not installed (run: sci2audio voices download)
    7    output files exist (add --overwrite to replace them)
    8    another sci2audio job is working on this file
    130  stopped with Ctrl-C
  
  '''
# ---
